    Fix for GHSA-6f53-jp7x-gg7p: Disable parsing jsessionid from url
    
    As reported in GHSA-6f53-jp7x-gg7p, spring parses the (arbitrary) value
    of the jsessionid from the URL if no other session cookie is already
    present.  This presents issues if you can trick a user into following a
    link with your malicious session id and then logging in, since it allows
    for a session hijack attack.
    
    Unclear if this is going to break any of our integrations, but barring
    those *requiring* that this be enabled, this seems like the correct fix.
